  "problem": "A many-to-many or ambiguous mapping could collapse to one preferred row silently. Unmatched keys and date scope could be dropped. Source-native IDs could be heuristically merged. A shared field name alone could produce a join route. Candidate routes could be treated as qualified before scoped validation and review. Editing sealed identity family-graph.mjs or join-routes.mjs would break WP7.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Crosswalks live in packages/enrichment/crosswalks.mjs with a thin re-export at scripts/research-program/crosswalks.mjs. Priority CCN/NPI/facility and geographic-vintage crosswalks store publisher, release, rights and exact access route. Entity and key-system mismatches fail closed. Absence of a crosswalk is explicit. One-to-many mappings, unmatched keys and date scope are preserved. A many-to-many or ambiguous mapping cannot collapse to one preferred row. Candidate routes remain candidate until scoped validation and review. A shared field name alone cannot produce a route. Mapping files are data products with their own versions. Sealed packages/identity/src/family-graph.mjs (4322 bytes) and join-routes.mjs (6287 bytes) are unchanged.",
